{
  "requirement": "`SourceProject` supplies the project files and domain mapping for a single agent request.\n\n```rust,ignore\npub struct SourceProject<D: Domain> { /* private fields */ }\n\nimpl<D: Domain> SourceProject<D> {\n    pub fn new(domain: D, sources: Sources) -> Self;\n    pub async fn search_text(&self, query: &TextQuery,) -> Result<SearchResults<SearchHit<NodeId<D>>>, SourceError>;\n    pub async fn search_structure(&self, query: &StructuralQuery,) -> Result<SearchResults<SearchHit<NodeId<D>>>, SourceError>;\n}\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Obligations.** `requirements.sdk.sources.SourceProject` says the type supplies the project files and the domain mapping for one agent request. It gives a public surface of `new(domain, sources)`, `search_text` and `search_structure`. Both searches return hits keyed by domain `NodeId<D>`. The text states no specific error conditions or limits. Scoping, grouping and tag semantics belong to the separate search requirements, which the same tests also mark.\n\n**Mapping to tests.**\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/project_sources.rs#mod[tests]/fn[search_groups_exact_occurrences_and_records_the_selected_declaration]`:\n  - It builds the project with `ProjectSources::new(project(\"\"), Sources::new(root))`, which is `SourceProject::new`.\n  - It calls `search_text` and asserts the exact hits: the domain node (`code.rs#const[A]` and `code.rs#const[B]`), the spans, and the text.\n  - This checks that file hits are mapped to domain nodes.\n  - It also asserts the agent-facing page, and that the dependency recorded for the selected hit is the domain node's fingerprint.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/project_sources.rs#mod[tests]/fn[structural_tags_select_only_the_original_enclosing_item]`:\n  - It calls `search_structure` on the project.\n  - It asserts the domain nodes (`code.rs#fn[one]` and `code.rs#fn[two]`), the spans, and the matched text. It compares the spans with the compiled rule run on the file contents.\n  - It also checks the result against the file as it was when searched, after the file is rewritten.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/configured.rs#mod[tests]/fn[configured_agent_uses_domain_source_tools_in_independent_executions]`:\n  - It covers the single-agent-request aspect end to end. A domain configured with `with_sources` exposes the source tools to the agent. The test runs two independent executions that each use list, read, search and finish.\n  - It asserts the tool set and the domain-mapped nodes. Each run's dependencies are asserted, as are the node IDs recorded for the files read. The mapping is reset per execution.\n  - This exercises the domain-supplied `project_sources`, which builds a `SourceProject` from the domain and its sources.\n\n**Gaps.** I found none. Both public search methods are tested with exact assertions on the domain node mapping. The constructor is used in a test, and the per-request supply of files and mapping is tested end to end. The text names no failure or boundary case beyond the `SourceError` return type, so no failure scenario is required. All three tests carry `{test}` references to the subject.",
  "references": "61d817e0045de305ffb7314d4e7fc908903dc4a8a5f601aee33454564d2e45e0",
